config:
  flowchart:
    wrappingWidth: 400
---
flowchart TB
    accTitle: What starts the bots
    accDescr: Renovate, the updates of Dependabot, the release bot and the branch bot merge as the release app, and a person as themselves, since a merge with the token of a workflow would start no workflow. So every merge into main is a push, which starts the release bot and the branch bot at once; they keep the release pull request current and bring the next pull request up to date. Only an event that GitHub lost waits for the schedules, a few runs a day, which GitHub runs as it can, often hours late, and every night the bot-health bot starts a workflow whose schedule GitHub missed.

    merge["Renovate, Dependabot's updates, the release bot and<br>the branch bot merge as the release app, a person as themselves"]
    push["The push to main starts the release bot<br>and the branch bot at once"]
    done["The release pull request is current,<br>the next pull request comes up to date"]
    lost["Only an event that GitHub lost waits for the schedules,<br>a few runs a day, often hours late"]
    health["Every night, the bot-health bot starts<br>a workflow whose schedule GitHub missed"]

    merge --> push
    push --> done
    done -.-> lost
    lost -.-> health

    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef person fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    class merge,push,lost,health bot
    class done done
